Plain-language summary (the terms below govern, not this summary):

  - Run it for yourself, your company or your clients' printing: allowed, free
    of charge, including commercially.
  - Read it, modify it, redistribute it: allowed.
  - Offer it to the public as a hosted or managed print service of your own:
    not allowed. That is the part the licensor intends to offer.

Two notes on scope:

  - Versions up to and including v1.4.0 were released under the MIT License and
    remain available under those terms; the MIT text is kept in LICENSE-MIT.
    This license applies to everything after v1.4.0.
  - The WooCommerce plugin in integrations/woocommerce/printpapi/ is licensed
    separately under the GNU General Public License v2 or later (see the LICENSE
    file in that directory), because WordPress plugins must be GPL-compatible.
    It only calls this software's HTTP API; it is not part of it.

